WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.334
-Ana, welcome back to the show.
-Thank you.

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:04.901
Happy new year.
-Happy new year!

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:06.234
Our first guest!

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:09.200
Our first guest of the new year!
That's good luck for us.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.000
-Yes.
-You know I always loved you,

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.601
but I heard something, and
now I even love you even more.

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:16.901
-Okay.
-Because I heard that you --

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:19.834
you like a certain ice cream.
-Oh.

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:21.467
-It's one of your favorite
ice creams?

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:23.267
-The only ice cream I like.

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:25.801
-The only ice cream you like
is The Tonight Dough.

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:28.067
-Yeah. That is true.
-This is our ice cream.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:29.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:31.434
This is Ben &amp; Jerry's.

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:34.434
-Yeah. It's all I eat.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.367
-That's -- I love that.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:38.133
It's the best ice cream, right?
-Just, like, every day.

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:39.968
When I'm on a diet,
when I'm not on a diet.

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:41.634
-It doesn't matter.
-It doesn't matter.

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:43.133
-No. You burn it off.
-Yeah. I do.

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:45.601
-It gives you the energy
you need to keep going

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:49.934
and keep Ana de Armas the way --
at the top of her game.

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:52.033
The Tonight Dough.
-That's the secret.

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:55.634
-Did you know, by the way --
100% of my proceeds from this

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:57.167
goes to SeriousFun.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:58.767
It's a great charity,
by the way.

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.000
Paul Newman. Joanne Woodward.
-That's awesome.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.534
-It's the best.
So it's a win-win.

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:05.133
-Yes.
-It is a win.

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:07.734
And I love that you --
-Why did you put it away?

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:11.267
-Oh, I have it right here.
Let's go. I can go --

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:13.167
-Okay.
-Absolutely. Yeah. Here.

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:15.501
-Don't judge me.
-We won't share.

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:17.567
Yeah. I've got my own over here.

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:19.567
-Oh, it's kind of melting.
So even better.

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:21.400
-It's even better!
I know! It is better!

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.334
I know. I can't stop.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.934
But the problem with this
is I start

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:28.701
and I really eat the whole --
I eat the whole thing.

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.434
-Mm-hmm.
-It's got cookies in there.

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:32.501
It's got cookie dough.
Peanut-butter cookie dough.

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:34.434
I mean, it's such an ad
for this, but why not?

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:37.133
It goes to a great cause.
It goes to a great cause.

00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:38.434
-To me, you know you've made it

00:01:38.434 --> 00:01:40.000
when you have
your own ice cream.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.701
-Yeah.
-I want my own ice cream.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.868
I want Ben &amp; Jerry's
to make my own flavor.

00:01:43.868 --> 00:01:45.400
-Yeah.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:47.601 --> 00:01:51.901
-The problem is...
it would be the same ice cream.

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:54.434
-Because you like this?
-Because this is better.

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:55.701
-No, but you could --

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:58.000
-Maybe just adding
condensed milk to it.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.100
-Ooh, condensed milk.
-I would still buy yours.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.167
-No. Wait. What could we add
for the Ana de Armas edition?

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:10.200
Maybe a blondie --
Like, you know, those --

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.267
-I don't know what blondie is.
This is very American.

00:02:12.267 --> 00:02:14.667
-Brownies. Brownies are --

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:18.534
Blondies are the, like, vanilla
cake version of brownies.

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:19.801
-Okay.
-So you can add that --

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:21.467
Like, would that work?
-Audience: Yeah.

00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:22.934
-Yeah. People like --

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:24.467
Ben and Jerry,
are you hearing this?

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:26.400
Let's make this work. Come on.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.667
By the way, you've been on
the show for "Bond" last time,

00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:31.467
and now you're on for "Blonde."

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:32.567
-I know.

00:02:32.567 --> 00:02:34.200
-One letter
every time you come on.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.968
[ Laughs ]
You are the greatest.

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:40.400
Congrats on this and congrats
on the Golden Globe nom.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.133
-Thank you.
-I mean, it's got to feel good.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:43.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:44.901
-Thank you so much.

00:02:44.901 --> 00:02:46.934
-It's got to feel good.
-Yeah.

00:02:46.934 --> 00:02:48.834
-Where were you when you
found out you got nominated?

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:50.701
-I was on set.

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:53.934
I'm still filming "Ballerina,"
the "John Wick" spin-off.

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:55.734
-Oh, yeah. Oh, with Ke-- Yeah.

00:02:55.734 --> 00:02:57.400
How's Keanu Reeves doing?

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:58.734
-He's awesome.

00:02:58.734 --> 00:03:00.367
I mean, Keanu is Keanu.
You know.

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:02.467
-He is the best, right?
He's a cool customer.

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:04.934
-We've been in Prague
filming for four months.

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:06.934
We still have
one more month to go.

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:08.934
-Wow.
-And I'm in pain.

00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:11.334
I'm not gonna --
You know, my body, my back.

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:12.667
Everything hurts.

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.367
I'm complaining.
I'm sore. I'm bruised.

00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:15.701
-You did action stuff in "Bond."

00:03:15.701 --> 00:03:18.634
-Well, "Bond" was 15 minutes.
This is a whole movie.

00:03:18.634 --> 00:03:20.167
Another level.

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:22.734
But the other day,
Keanu and I were rehearsing

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:25.834
our very difficult stunt scene,

00:03:25.834 --> 00:03:28.133
and this man is just rolling

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:31.968
and throwing me
and doing these crazy stunts.

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:34.567
And I'm like --
I can't complain anymore.

00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:36.033
I'm done.

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:37.968
-Why?
-Because he is doing it!

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:40.267
-And he doesn't complain?
-No, never.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.133
He's just...
-Keanu.

00:03:42.133 --> 00:03:43.868
-He truly is the best,
and he's always --

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:45.601
-Can't you just complain
about one thing,

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:47.267
say, "Oh, my back hurt me
on that one"?

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:48.601
-No.
-He doesn't say anything?

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:51.501
-No. Nothing. Never.
So I'm like, "Okay."

00:03:51.501 --> 00:03:53.834
-"Okay. This is fun. Yeah.
We're just doing it."

00:03:53.834 --> 00:03:55.968
So then you're on set,
and what do you get?

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:57.834
-Oh, sorry.
That was the question.

00:03:57.834 --> 00:03:59.300
-No. I love it.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.968
-So, I'm on set, and they were
just, like, in between takes.

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:03.667
They're changing lenses
or something,

00:04:03.667 --> 00:04:05.367
and my assistant
comes with a phone,

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:07.734
like, very straight-faced
and just gives me something

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:09.667
to read,
and it was this text chain.

00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:12.167
And I start reading,
and then I realized

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:13.801
what I'm reading, and I scream.

00:04:13.801 --> 00:04:15.400
But, of course,
it was a stunt scene,

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.000
so everyone got very worried

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.701
thinking that something
was happening.

00:04:18.701 --> 00:04:20.467
I was, like, "No, no, no, no.
It's okay."

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:21.701
-"No, no. This is great news.

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:23.267
-I got nominated
for a Golden Globe!

00:04:23.267 --> 00:04:25.200
Yeah, this is great news."

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.133
-So...yeah.
It was pretty cool.

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:33.067
-You knocked it out of the park,
unbelievably.

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:36.133
I can't even imagine how tough
it is to play this role.

00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:38.601
-Thank you.
-You're playing Marilyn Monroe.

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:42.267
And the story behind
what we know of Marilyn Monroe,

00:04:42.267 --> 00:04:44.734
it's like --
it's a pretty dark take on this.

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:46.334
-Yeah.
-You're phenomenal.

00:04:46.334 --> 00:04:48.234
Let me just show everyone
a picture.

00:04:48.234 --> 00:04:52.767
This is you and also
another screenshot of Marilyn.

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:54.701
That is unbelievable.
-Yeah.

00:04:54.701 --> 00:04:58.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:58.267 --> 00:05:01.300
-I mean, did you
have to do every take,

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.434
like, a thousand times

00:05:03.434 --> 00:05:05.067
just to make sure
you got it perfect?

00:05:05.067 --> 00:05:06.767
-A lot of times, yeah. Yeah.

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:09.334
Andrew is a very --
is an incredible filmmaker

00:05:09.334 --> 00:05:12.167
and also very detailed
and precise.

00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:15.434
And it was really important
for him and me

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:19.033
and every department
to really nail this re-creation.

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:22.968
And so we had two monitors,

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:25.501
our movie
and then Marilyn's movie,

00:05:25.501 --> 00:05:28.534
and they were playing
both at the same time,

00:05:28.534 --> 00:05:30.667
and if we didn't get it right,
we had to do it again.

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:33.200
-Really?
-I mean, it was so accurate.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.868
There was a moment
where my hairstylist

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:39.634
kept coming back and forth to me
and the monitor to fix my hair.

00:05:39.634 --> 00:05:42.067
And she was -- poor thing --
doing so many trips

00:05:42.067 --> 00:05:44.367
that I'd just go with her
to the monitors.

00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:46.000
-Yeah.
"Show me what the problem is."

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.300
-Yeah. "What is going on?"

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:50.634
And I realized
that she is looking at Marilyn

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.467
trying to fix my hair.

00:05:52.467 --> 00:05:53.868
-She wasn't even looking at you.

00:05:53.868 --> 00:05:55.033
-Yeah, she wasn't looking at me.

00:05:55.033 --> 00:05:56.234
-"I'm on this monitor."

00:05:56.234 --> 00:05:58.534
You're like, "Oh, okay."
Oh, my God. Wow.

00:05:58.534 --> 00:06:00.400
-So, yeah, it is a testament
to, you know...

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.300
-They did such an amazing job.
Perfectionists.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:04.200
-...the incredible work
that the art department

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:05.767
and hair and makeup
and wardrobe did.

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:07.200
-Choreography,
the way it looked.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.067
The lighting was unbelievable.

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:11.801
And you do this and you go,

00:06:11.801 --> 00:06:14.334
"Okay, I think
I have a take on this

00:06:14.334 --> 00:06:16.067
and how to do this scene."

00:06:16.067 --> 00:06:17.801
And do you remember
the first scene you did

00:06:17.801 --> 00:06:20.734
where you were like, "Alright.
Action. And here we go.

00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:22.067
And let's see if, you know..."

00:06:22.067 --> 00:06:23.901
-Well, it was
a pretty tough scene.

00:06:23.901 --> 00:06:26.067
Andrew didn't, you know,
give me, like,

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:28.234
a slow "breaking the ice" thing.

00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:30.901
We just went for a, you know,

00:06:30.901 --> 00:06:33.100
very long dialogue scene
with the mother.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:37.434
So -- And, you know,
we didn't have any rehearsals.

00:06:37.434 --> 00:06:42.133
Andrew had never heard me
speaking or moving like Marilyn,

00:06:42.133 --> 00:06:46.267
so I just went to set and
I did this very intense scene,

00:06:46.267 --> 00:06:49.434
and it was the first time
for everyone

00:06:49.434 --> 00:06:51.801
to hear me and see me
playing Marilyn.

00:06:51.801 --> 00:06:53.868
And it was terrifying.

00:06:53.868 --> 00:06:55.133
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:55.133 --> 00:06:57.501
-Well, "Blonde" takes --

00:06:57.501 --> 00:06:59.634
Like we said,
it's a take on Marilyn.

00:06:59.634 --> 00:07:01.801
How else
can we describe this movie

00:07:01.801 --> 00:07:03.434
for anyone who hasn't seen it?

00:07:03.434 --> 00:07:07.834
-I think this is a movie
more about Norma Jean.

00:07:07.834 --> 00:07:09.767
-Yeah.
-The person who --

00:07:09.767 --> 00:07:14.467
The woman who's been unseen,
you know, this whole time.

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:17.501
And I feel like
this photographic memory

00:07:17.501 --> 00:07:19.801
that we have of Marilyn's life.
-Yeah.

00:07:19.801 --> 00:07:21.701
-All these images
that we've seen

00:07:21.701 --> 00:07:24.400
and we have an idea
of what that story was.

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:28.334
It's kind of like a take on that

00:07:28.334 --> 00:07:31.868
through her lens and what
her life was like, so...

00:07:31.868 --> 00:07:33.567
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:33.567 --> 00:07:36.334
Here's Ana de Armas in "Blonde."
Take a look at this.

00:07:36.334 --> 00:07:37.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:37.868 --> 00:07:39.434
-[ Sobbing ] Please.

00:07:39.434 --> 00:07:42.667
-She's coming.
-Please come.

00:07:42.667 --> 00:07:45.601
-She's coming.

00:07:45.601 --> 00:07:47.567
-Don't abandon me.

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:49.734
-She's coming.

00:07:49.734 --> 00:07:51.701
She's almost here.

00:07:51.701 --> 00:07:54.901
-[ Sniffles ] Please come.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:01.033
♪♪

00:08:01.033 --> 00:08:02.968
[ Sniffles ]

00:08:02.968 --> 00:08:09.067
♪♪

00:08:09.067 --> 00:08:15.167
♪♪

00:08:15.167 --> 00:08:17.267
[ Giggling ]

00:08:17.267 --> 00:08:19.334
[ Crowd chanting "Marilyn" ]

00:08:19.334 --> 00:08:24.334
♪♪

00:08:24.334 --> 00:08:25.634
[ Smooches ]

00:08:25.634 --> 00:08:27.133
-Ooph!

00:08:27.133 --> 00:08:29.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:29.167 --> 00:08:31.434
Transform into -- Oh, my gosh.

00:08:31.434 --> 00:08:33.901
Ana de Armas, everybody!

00:08:33.901 --> 00:08:37.067
"Blonde" is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:08:37.067 --> 00:08:39.033
Ana and I are playing a new game
when we come back.

00:08:39.033 --> 00:08:41.133
Stick around, everybody.

